      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T13:53:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree; offsetof and CType look a little awkward in the uniform definition, but I think it wins out for conciseness and makes the uniform value writing a lot simpler.\n\nI also like that it makes the uniform data spec directly connected to the C++ code, so if those values are re-arranged, etc., it just works. There\u0027s no magic offsets or indices that the GrProc has to remember to use or update.\n\nGiven that, I think this direction should be further fleshed out and am liking that the multi-virtual GrUniformWriter is gone.",
      "parentUuid": "3b43c384_19f4dc4e",
      "revId": "a639efdc708776da77a37204c246b416b9f45e18",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
